      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes **how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure**.\n\nSpecifically, it explains that before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records that file\u0027s prior state \u2014 either its previous content (if it existed) or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist \u2014 into an in-memory write journal. If an agent run fails for any reason (turn cap exceeded, unrecoverable error, or write denial), the journal can roll every recorded write back in reverse order: restoring previous content for files that existed, and deleting newly created files. This gives each run all-or-nothing semantics for its writes without requiring a database transaction.\n\nThe page also notes that the Query agent never uses this rollback path since it has no write tool, though the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library.",
